WEBVTT

01:30.170 --> 01:35.130
<b><u>Episode 8
</u>Surprise</b>

01:32.850 --> 01:34.860
Did you bring your change of clothes?

01:34.860 --> 01:35.320
Yes.

01:35.690 --> 01:36.700
And your toothbrush?

01:35.690 --> 01:37.950
I can help whoever is next.

01:37.000 --> 01:37.950
I've got it.

01:37.950 --> 01:39.840
Oh, your passport!

01:39.840 --> 01:41.450
I have it... I promise.

01:42.090 --> 01:43.540
I've confirmed this, as well.

01:44.040 --> 01:45.010
She's fine.

01:45.560 --> 01:47.040
I'm fine.

01:47.520 --> 01:51.250
I am, um... a hero, after all.

01:52.700 --> 01:54.090
You're right.

01:54.670 --> 01:56.870
Okay, have a good trip.

01:56.870 --> 01:57.840
Thanks.

02:01.360 --> 02:03.670
<i>Hello, everyone in Japan.</i>

02:05.740 --> 02:09.900
<i>I'm currently... in Russia.</i>

02:12.080 --> 02:18.560
<i>Because a member of Amarariruku seems 
to look very familiar to Pepesha-san.</i>

02:20.010 --> 02:24.630
<i>To investigate this, I'm heading over to 
meet with Pepesha-san in her homeland,</i>

02:25.120 --> 02:26.490
<i>but...</i>

02:27.740 --> 02:29.680
<i>Isn't Pepesha-san here yet?</i>

02:30.170 --> 02:33.670
<i>Honestly, being in another 
country alone is a bit scawy...</i>

02:31.710 --> 02:33.670
Alone...

02:34.120 --> 02:35.430
Teru-chan!

02:36.850 --> 02:38.840
Thanks for coming so far.

02:39.200 --> 02:40.590
Pepesha-san!

02:41.040 --> 02:43.350
Is your wound doing better?

02:43.650 --> 02:48.480
Oh, I'm totally fine now. 
I'm all warm, and I feel great.

02:48.480 --> 02:52.240
And now you're here, too, so I'm super happy.

02:52.240 --> 02:54.270
Okay, let's go.

02:55.360 --> 02:57.020
<i>She's drunk.</i>

03:00.110 --> 03:04.370
P-Pepesha-san, are you always drinking?

03:05.920 --> 03:09.540
Oh, come on, Teru-chan! You're making 
it sound like I'm sick or something.

03:09.800 --> 03:13.690
I knew I was seeing you today, 
so I made sure I was drunk!

03:13.690 --> 03:15.380
Because you were seeing me?

03:17.960 --> 03:21.580
Teru-chan, if you saw me sober,

03:21.580 --> 03:24.780
you probably wouldn't recognize me.

03:24.780 --> 03:25.700
Huh?!

03:28.160 --> 03:31.770
Um, where are we going?

03:31.770 --> 03:34.650
We're heading to the place where I grew up.

03:34.920 --> 03:41.240
They'll have old photo albums there,
and I thought that might be helpful for research.

03:41.700 --> 03:45.410
What were you like as a child, Pepesha-san?

03:45.840 --> 03:50.750
Well... I wasn't a very cheerful child.

03:50.750 --> 03:53.480
Huh... That's kind of surprising.

03:53.480 --> 03:55.920
Really? Actually, that's fair!

03:58.380 --> 03:59.680
We're here.

04:04.550 --> 04:05.720
What's this place?

04:06.160 --> 04:07.870
Yuri Orphanage.

04:07.870 --> 04:09.720
This is where I grew up.

04:10.170 --> 04:12.080
U-Um...

04:12.080 --> 04:15.600
Don't worry! Everyone's super nice!

04:15.600 --> 04:19.230
Well, well, I think I hear 
some cheerful voices.

04:19.640 --> 04:23.610
Welcome back, Pesha... My beloved daughter.

04:23.610 --> 04:25.070
Mr. Isaak!

04:26.210 --> 04:27.720
It's been so long!

04:30.320 --> 04:32.090
And who's this?

04:32.090 --> 04:34.580
This is Teru Momijiyama-chan from Japan.

04:35.030 --> 04:36.840
She's my friend.

04:36.840 --> 04:41.140
Oh... H-Hello. Thank you for having me.

04:41.140 --> 04:43.330
It's nice to meet you.

04:43.330 --> 04:46.790
Welcome to Yuri Orphanage.

04:46.790 --> 04:48.810
My name is Isaak.

04:48.810 --> 04:51.130
I'm the director here.

04:51.130 --> 04:54.060
You're so young, but you 
speak our language so well.

04:55.020 --> 04:56.970
Th-Thank you.

04:57.810 --> 05:01.320
<b>Heart-shift 
Bracelets</b>

04:57.810 --> 05:01.320
She's using her Heart-shift 
bracelets' powers to translate.

05:02.160 --> 05:04.480
Enough talking out here.

05:04.480 --> 05:06.610
Let's head on in.

05:07.190 --> 05:09.370
Everyone's waiting for you.

05:13.850 --> 05:16.510
All right, kids. Say hello to our guests.

05:16.510 --> 05:18.500
Pepesha-san's back.

05:18.870 --> 05:20.400
What? Pesha-san?!

05:20.400 --> 05:21.090
Really?

05:21.670 --> 05:24.730
Hi! How are you all doing?

05:26.070 --> 05:27.070
Why'd you come back?

05:27.070 --> 05:29.440
We got all the books you sent us!

05:28.560 --> 05:30.100
The snacks were yummy, too.

05:30.100 --> 05:31.710
Thanks for always sending them!

05:31.710 --> 05:34.600
No problem. You all seem to be doing well.

05:35.140 --> 05:37.850
<i>Pepesha-san's really popular here, too.</i>

05:38.170 --> 05:41.810
So where did you meet Pesha, Teru-san?

05:41.810 --> 05:44.050
Huh? Uh, um...

05:44.490 --> 05:49.030
W-We're sort of like colleagues.

05:49.030 --> 05:50.200
I see.

05:50.750 --> 05:54.980
She never really tells me about her work,

05:54.980 --> 05:58.160
but I'm glad she's got someone like you.

05:58.160 --> 06:00.290
Oh... Th-Thank you.

06:01.100 --> 06:04.590
It's been ten years since Pesha left,

06:04.590 --> 06:08.320
but she still seems pretty 
concerned about us.

06:08.320 --> 06:11.800
She always sends us money once a month.

06:12.960 --> 06:17.600
Thanks to that, we're still 
able to run our orphanage.

06:18.390 --> 06:22.360
Though she's never told me 
what kind of work she does...

06:22.630 --> 06:27.010
She's a hero to all of the kids here.

06:29.120 --> 06:29.940
Right.

06:34.160 --> 06:36.800
Here are the albums from 
when you were still here.

06:36.800 --> 06:38.500
Thank you very much!

06:38.820 --> 06:42.710
But what do you need them for?

06:42.710 --> 06:45.700
I'm investigating something 
that happened back then.

06:45.700 --> 06:48.510
I was wondering what kind of child I was.

06:49.650 --> 06:51.820
Well, make yourselves at home.

06:51.820 --> 06:53.890
More importantly, Pesha...

06:54.880 --> 06:57.520
It seems you like alcohol, too,

06:58.200 --> 06:59.730
but don't overdo it.

07:02.230 --> 07:03.820
Yes, sir.

07:09.750 --> 07:13.900
Hmm... I wonder if we'll find anything.

07:14.960 --> 07:15.870
Um...

07:16.480 --> 07:18.350
I know it's late to say this, but...

07:18.350 --> 07:22.330
I had no idea you grew up in an orphanage.

07:22.630 --> 07:27.500
Yup. I was taken into this 
orphanage when I was twelve,

07:28.480 --> 07:32.090
and I stayed here for five 
years until I was seventeen.

07:33.200 --> 07:34.700
Nice place, right?

07:35.200 --> 07:37.600
Everyone here is so warm and kind.

07:38.600 --> 07:42.710
And because of that, I was 
really lonely when I left.

07:43.600 --> 07:46.590
But, I mean, I come back every now and then,

07:46.590 --> 07:48.550
so I haven't completely left the nest.

07:49.280 --> 07:50.780
Oh, look, Teru-chan!

07:51.140 --> 07:52.910
It's me.

07:52.910 --> 07:54.280
Where?

07:54.870 --> 07:55.790
Right here.

07:57.830 --> 08:03.220
Oh, my gosh! I'm so grumpy! 
My personality must've sucked!

08:03.220 --> 08:05.170
I-I'm sure that's not true.

08:05.580 --> 08:07.790
You look very cute.

08:08.500 --> 08:09.550
Do I?

08:09.830 --> 08:13.550
But look. I'm just so grumpy.

08:15.180 --> 08:18.210
Oh, you're smiling in this picture.

08:19.020 --> 08:20.440
What even is that face?

08:20.440 --> 08:22.800
Why couldn't I smile better?

08:23.610 --> 08:29.700
But... you do sort of look like 
that Tzveta girl, if only vaguely.

08:29.700 --> 08:33.390
Do I? I guess this isn't enough to tell.

08:33.390 --> 08:34.850
Let's find more pictures.

08:35.900 --> 08:37.820
Oh, something just fell out.

08:38.070 --> 08:39.810
Huh, I wonder what it is.

08:43.380 --> 08:45.030
What's that?

08:45.560 --> 08:46.880
This is...

08:47.590 --> 08:49.700
a picture of my mama.

08:50.670 --> 08:53.190
A picture of your mother?

08:53.650 --> 08:57.140
Yes. I guess it was between the pages.

08:57.930 --> 08:59.160
This takes me back.

09:01.870 --> 09:03.020
That's right...

09:04.440 --> 09:06.270
I think, when I first got here...

09:07.660 --> 09:10.140
I carried this picture around 
with me everywhere.

09:12.750 --> 09:15.150
I felt all alone.

09:16.870 --> 09:20.020
You must've really loved your mother.

09:20.730 --> 09:24.010
Yes, and I admired her, too.

09:24.010 --> 09:26.960
She raised me all by herself.

09:27.740 --> 09:30.550
Mama also was raised in this orphanage,

09:30.550 --> 09:33.960
and that's how I was able to get in.

09:34.870 --> 09:36.380
She never really said much.

09:36.910 --> 09:41.220
But there were occasionally nights 
when she was really talkative.

09:42.100 --> 09:43.350
Do you know why?

09:43.910 --> 09:45.700
Why? I...

09:47.350 --> 09:48.270
Yup!

09:48.700 --> 09:50.770
Because she was wasted.

09:52.310 --> 09:54.780
My mama was always stoic and cool,

09:55.340 --> 09:59.490
but when she drank, she was like 
a really talkative and cute friend.

10:01.080 --> 10:04.330
And that's why, back then, I thought...

10:05.470 --> 10:11.110
that alcohol was a magic medicine that 
allowed adults to return to being children.

10:14.000 --> 10:16.340
And that's exactly why kids 
aren't allowed to drink it!

10:16.800 --> 10:19.560
Because then you'd turn into a baby 
and eventually just disappear!

10:21.310 --> 10:23.110
I see. In that case...

10:23.110 --> 10:27.770
I guess you must've taken after 
your mother, Pepesha-san.

10:29.810 --> 10:31.480
Huh? Have I?

10:31.480 --> 10:34.650
I mean... judging from everything 
you've told me so far...

10:34.980 --> 10:37.950
Y-You know... Like the fact 
that you both like alcohol,

10:37.950 --> 10:40.660
how you're both cute when you're drunk...

10:41.150 --> 10:45.730
Oh, come on. Everyone 
around here is like that.

10:45.730 --> 10:46.620
Um...

10:47.980 --> 10:49.170
Yes?

10:50.940 --> 10:53.250
Did you find what you were looking for?

10:53.250 --> 10:54.210
Sir.

10:54.940 --> 10:57.490
It's already past noon.

10:57.490 --> 10:59.340
Why don't you have some lunch?

11:03.380 --> 11:05.060
Ah, that was so tasty.

11:05.440 --> 11:06.850
Thank you for the meal.

11:07.120 --> 11:10.720
Sir, do you happen to have any beer?

11:11.300 --> 11:14.720
Pesha... You need to know when to stop.

11:14.720 --> 11:15.980
Aw...

11:16.290 --> 11:20.420
Hey, you there. Is this 
what you're looking for?

11:20.420 --> 11:22.990
Hm? This voice that makes 
the earth tremble...

11:23.610 --> 11:25.280
Natalia-san!

11:26.500 --> 11:27.980
It's been so long!

11:27.980 --> 11:29.680
Wait, did you gain weight again?

11:29.680 --> 11:32.690
Really? If you're gonna say stuff 
like that, you don't get any.

11:32.690 --> 11:36.250
Oh, no! I'm kidding! You're the 
most beautiful and the best!

11:36.950 --> 11:40.060
Oh, Teru-chan. This is Natalia-san.

11:40.060 --> 11:42.960
She's been staff here since I was here.

11:42.960 --> 11:45.650
Are you the girlie who came from Japan?

11:45.650 --> 11:47.680
I-I'm Teru Momijiyama.

11:48.050 --> 11:51.690
Well, there sure isn't a lot around 
here, but make yourself at home.

11:51.690 --> 11:54.020
Th-Thank you...

11:55.500 --> 11:57.190
Now then, Pesha...

11:57.730 --> 11:59.860
Right then, Natalia.

11:59.860 --> 12:02.400
Yeah!

12:03.740 --> 12:05.530
W-Wow...

12:07.560 --> 12:12.790
So, what? You two came to 
take a trip down memory lane?

12:12.790 --> 12:13.420
Yes.

12:14.330 --> 12:18.740
When I was going through the albums, 
I remembered a lot from my time here.

12:19.360 --> 12:21.920
It felt really nostalgic.

12:22.290 --> 12:25.730
You were pretty awful 
when you first came here.

12:25.730 --> 12:27.890
You wouldn't say a damn word.

12:27.890 --> 12:29.780
Really?

12:30.760 --> 12:34.550
But you're starting to look 
more and more like Lenya.

12:34.550 --> 12:38.440
She only smiled when she was drinking, though.

12:39.700 --> 12:41.010
Lenya?

12:41.690 --> 12:43.950
Letana Andreanova.

12:45.040 --> 12:47.200
That's my mama's name.

12:47.890 --> 12:51.090
When I was living here as an orphan,

12:51.090 --> 12:55.450
her mother, Lenya, was also here.

12:55.450 --> 12:58.170
You're also from here, Natalia-san?

12:58.500 --> 12:59.680
I sure am.

12:59.680 --> 13:02.570
Well, I guess in my case, I came right back.

13:05.270 --> 13:11.910
People told me they couldn't trust someone 
who had no parents to do any work.

13:12.400 --> 13:16.190
On top of that, I didn't 
have any schooling, either.

13:16.810 --> 13:19.940
Which is why I came right back here.

13:20.910 --> 13:24.270
People talk about how the wars are 
over now, stuff about heroes...

13:24.270 --> 13:26.820
Everyone talks about how the 
world's supposedly changed...

13:27.170 --> 13:31.830
But the little corners of the world haven't 
changed. It's still a struggle to survive.

13:32.170 --> 13:36.240
Oh, I'm sorry. That was probably pretty boring.

13:36.240 --> 13:38.000
Oh, no! Not at all.

13:38.580 --> 13:42.560
Oh, right. You're looking for 
old memories, aren't you?

13:42.560 --> 13:45.340
Why don't you have a look at my albums, too?

13:45.340 --> 13:50.660
Good point. I'm pretty sure 
Lenya would be in those.

13:51.350 --> 13:55.440
I'd love to see when all of you were kids!

13:55.440 --> 13:57.450
Bring them out already!

13:57.450 --> 13:59.320
Oh, all right, then.

14:01.840 --> 14:03.070
Here you go.

14:03.430 --> 14:06.030
Well, let's have a look...

14:06.030 --> 14:08.570
Oh, look! I'm right here.

14:09.070 --> 14:10.890
This takes me back!

14:10.890 --> 14:13.160
Which one are you, Natalia-san?

14:13.570 --> 14:14.740
I'm right here.

14:24.630 --> 14:25.440
No way!

14:25.440 --> 14:27.020
What do you mean by that?!

14:27.020 --> 14:30.050
B-But your face is totally different!

14:30.320 --> 14:33.380
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow...

14:30.320 --> 14:35.300
What's that supposed to mean, huh, Pesha?!

14:33.380 --> 14:37.180
I mean... Y-You were really pretty!

14:35.300 --> 14:37.180
Go on. Say that again.

14:37.180 --> 14:41.790
Ow, ow, ow! Natalia-san, please stop!

14:38.370 --> 14:41.030
What? Had enough?

14:41.030 --> 14:43.190
<i>They must be very close.</i>

14:43.940 --> 14:47.910
<i>But Natalia-san looked like a 
princess when she was younger.</i>

14:47.910 --> 14:50.450
<i>The girl next to her is pretty, too...</i>

14:56.500 --> 14:58.620
So nostalgic...

15:00.620 --> 15:03.840
Come on, now. You're messing up my hair.

15:02.170 --> 15:03.840
Natalia-san...

15:03.840 --> 15:06.570
Is the girl standing next to you...

15:07.670 --> 15:11.340
Oh, that's right. That's Lenya.

15:11.770 --> 15:13.180
Sorry, could you get that?

15:13.180 --> 15:13.950
Yeah!

15:19.630 --> 15:22.830
Can I play with you, too?

15:23.860 --> 15:24.940
Which means...

15:24.940 --> 15:27.440
That's Pepesha's mother.

15:27.830 --> 15:30.070
Pepesha-san, look...

15:31.160 --> 15:32.170
Why...

15:32.870 --> 15:35.450
Why does Mama as a child...

15:36.320 --> 15:38.630
have the same face as that girl?

15:44.690 --> 15:45.570
Shy.

15:47.550 --> 15:50.970
<u>Tzveta Kooriskaya
Nationality: ???? 
 Likes: Cold ice, warm fire
A member of Amarariruku who
has the power to control ice.</u>

15:51.790 --> 15:54.060
Mama didn't have any family.

15:54.700 --> 15:57.470
She'd also be too young to be her sister.

15:58.070 --> 16:00.710
But in this picture...

16:01.860 --> 16:03.490
They look too much alike.

16:03.490 --> 16:04.890
It's like she's actually her.

16:06.500 --> 16:08.340
But my mama...

16:09.390 --> 16:10.600
Mama has...

16:11.660 --> 16:13.040
already left this world...

16:18.720 --> 16:19.790
What was that?!

16:20.850 --> 16:22.290
Don't tell me...

16:32.290 --> 16:33.940
What in the world is going on?

16:36.260 --> 16:38.960
What happened, little ones?

16:39.900 --> 16:41.600
W-We don't know...

16:42.240 --> 16:45.770
Th-This girl we don't know came up to us...

16:46.180 --> 16:48.020
And she froze them.

16:49.210 --> 16:50.610
What is...

16:51.040 --> 16:53.320
Teru-chan. We need to Heart-shift.

16:55.360 --> 16:56.190
Hurry!

16:56.190 --> 16:57.700
Oh, r-right!

17:12.960 --> 17:15.100
Teru-chan, take care of 
the kids who are down.

17:15.100 --> 17:16.260
R-Right!

17:17.280 --> 17:18.470
Pesha...

17:18.890 --> 17:21.720
<i>This ice... Don't tell me that girl...</i>

17:22.320 --> 17:24.550
<i>If she's here now, of all times...</i>

17:26.260 --> 17:27.840
<i>Is she after me?</i>

17:31.780 --> 17:33.500
A-Are you all right?

17:34.800 --> 17:36.510
So... so...

17:36.510 --> 17:37.200
Are you cold?

17:37.760 --> 17:39.340
Everything's okay now.

17:39.790 --> 17:40.450
Huh?

17:40.850 --> 17:42.990
<i>The way this girl is dressed...</i>

17:42.990 --> 17:44.950
So... so...

17:45.310 --> 17:47.960
Surprise!

17:51.090 --> 17:53.350
Well?! Was that funny?!

17:53.350 --> 17:56.340
Was it fun how I was all frozen?!

17:58.550 --> 18:00.540
I'm Kufufu-san!

18:01.220 --> 18:05.270
I was born to make sure 
the whole world's smiling!

18:05.850 --> 18:08.600
And then I'm going to kill 
everyone with laughter!

18:08.600 --> 18:09.850
JK!

18:10.890 --> 18:14.210
D-Do you belong to Amarariruku?

18:14.210 --> 18:17.990
What? You want to know about me?

18:19.130 --> 18:22.370
Why, yes. I belong to Amarariruku.

18:22.820 --> 18:25.600
You're not the only one 
here right now, are you?

18:25.600 --> 18:27.460
Tzveta's here, too, isn't she?

18:27.700 --> 18:30.240
Tzveta-chan? Yeah, she's here.

18:30.240 --> 18:33.180
You see, you see... We're here
because Tzveta-chan's...

18:33.670 --> 18:34.300
Huh?

18:34.980 --> 18:37.490
You'll probably end up 
telling them everything.

18:39.440 --> 18:41.300
Hello, Pesha.

18:41.960 --> 18:43.980
I'm happy to see you again.

18:45.460 --> 18:48.590
Sorry about last time.

18:48.590 --> 18:52.560
But you did something mean, 
like an adult would.

18:53.170 --> 18:56.570
Tzveta, why are you here?

18:57.360 --> 18:59.100
<i>She does resemble Mama.</i>

18:59.760 --> 19:01.220
<i>But that's impossible.</i>

19:02.850 --> 19:05.830
<i>Stigma takes advantage of the 
darkness in people's hearts.</i>

19:07.500 --> 19:10.380
<i>It wouldn't be surprising if he was 
trying to take advantage of my heart.</i>

19:12.870 --> 19:14.910
<i>There has to be some trick...</i>

19:16.350 --> 19:19.340
Why am I here, huh?

19:20.040 --> 19:24.700
You see... I don't remember anything 
before waking up at the North Pole.

19:25.990 --> 19:28.100
So I wonder why...

19:28.770 --> 19:34.110
I happen to remember you and 
this place just a little bit.

19:35.440 --> 19:38.920
I wonder if I cared a lot about you...

19:39.860 --> 19:42.950
Or perhaps I hated you...

19:43.240 --> 19:46.480
That's enough! Just who are you?!

19:46.480 --> 19:48.870
Why do you look like Mama?

19:49.530 --> 19:55.960
Mama, huh? I wonder if that's why 
I keep wanting to call you Pesha.

20:02.180 --> 20:05.030
If you keep mocking my mama 
with that imitation,

20:05.030 --> 20:06.990
I'm going to get angry!

20:06.990 --> 20:09.010
How strange.

20:09.010 --> 20:13.520
When I look at you, my heart feels restless.

20:14.160 --> 20:17.750
There are only a few things I remember,

20:18.220 --> 20:21.530
but I very much approve of Stigma's ideas.

20:22.180 --> 20:26.050
I'm pretty sure I hated this world.

20:26.720 --> 20:30.990
This cold world... overflowing 
with pain and suffering.

20:32.640 --> 20:36.770
But this place is so warm...

20:37.230 --> 20:40.260
I wanted to live here forever.

20:40.840 --> 20:43.680
The nostalgic landscape of my heart,

20:43.680 --> 20:46.550
embraced by the gentle wind...

20:47.520 --> 20:52.560
Ah... I knew this was it. This is my place.

20:53.370 --> 20:54.950
Your place?

20:55.590 --> 20:57.060
He told me...

20:57.670 --> 21:01.360
that within everyone's hearts 
is an impenetrable territory

21:01.360 --> 21:04.400
that's separate from reality.

21:06.340 --> 21:10.490
No suffering or pain exists there.

21:11.100 --> 21:11.830
It's only...

21:12.600 --> 21:14.940
filled with peace.

21:17.290 --> 21:22.590
And this is what he named that place...

21:26.900 --> 21:27.950
The sky...

21:36.640 --> 21:39.110
Amarariruku.

21:39.580 --> 21:43.160
I hate the cold reality.

21:44.390 --> 21:47.340
Let's spend all of our days within...

21:49.320 --> 21:51.610
the warm days of our youth forever.

21:55.180 --> 22:03.100
Welcome to the Amarariruku of my heart.
